ABSTRACT:
This paper evaluates discrete-event simulation techniques for uncovering Byzantine and asymmetric partition race conditions in Raft consensus. We present an event-driven execution harness decoupled from wall-clock time that guarantees deterministic reproduction of split-vote loops and state machine truncation anomalies.

1. INTRODUCTION
Distributed consensus algorithms must maintain safety invariants despite network partitions, message reordering, and arbitrary process pauses...
